cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Jaddle in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Jaddle: The JAX Saddle Solver"
abstract: >-
  First-order primal-dual solvers for large-scale linear and convex programs,
  written in JAX. Jaddle provides a restarted, adaptively step-sized
  PDHG-family solver for sparse linear programs and a general solver for
  smooth convex programs defined by JAX functions. Both run on CPU, GPU and
  TPU, and support batched and differentiable solves.
authors:
  - family-names: "van Rooyen"
    given-names: "Brendan"
version: 0.3.1
date-released: 2026-11-09
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/BrendanVR/Jaddle"
url: "https://github.com/BrendanVR/Jaddle"
keywords:
  - optimization
  - linear programming
  - convex optimization
  - PDHG
  - PDLP
  - saddle point
  - JAX
  - GPU
